Subject: [PATCH] dtl: retain upload bursts with configurable idle hysteresis

The balanced 32 MiB completed-upload cap repeatedly destroyed 33 of 48 staging
buffers in a measured 99 MiB Apple Silicon burst, tripling upload creation
latency. Admit a bounded 128 MiB burst for two seconds of successful workload
activity, then reclaim completed buffers to the 32 MiB soft cap on the next
pool operation. Keep pending fences protected, release completed burst excess
on OOM before existing fallback waits, and drain completed entries at teardown.
Explicit bounded decimal settings permit constrained-device experiments;
telemetry publishes the policy. Automatic balanced promotion stays disabled.

